			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				122,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Maintain): Add two-phase rustdoc quality rewrite scripts\n\nAdd two Python automation scripts under Maintain/_rewrite_docs.py and _rewrite_docs_phase2.py that apply systematic rustdoc comment quality fixes across the entire Maintain Source tree.\n\nPhase 1 handles surface-level patterns: removing \"This function/struct/enum\" meta-text to make doc comments direct, normalizing section headers from # to ## (Arguments→Parameters, Returns, Errors, Panics, Example, Behavior), and stripping block-comment section banners (// ===, // ---) that had been mistakenly included in doc comments.\n\nPhase 2 addresses structural issues: fixing lines with too many slashes (//// → //), correcting // comments accidentally prefixed as /// doc comments, and normalizing section banner markers.\n\nTogether the two scripts process all .rs files in Source/ and report a summary of modifications. This provides a repeatable, automated approach to maintaining rustdoc quality rather than requiring manual edits across hundreds of files.",
			"SHA": "b10db76e89c26f2ea04e9c66f4872ff4a8c54754"
		}
